{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790445849,"nonce":"4bMdDOs2Y38Xvta4RLX6jQHPWB4=","title":"Typed dicts: shape classes merge every dict of one structural shape","message":"Dict and set stores are decided per class of shapes that inference\njoined, and a shape is its (key, value) types program-wide. Joining\nDict(Str, Int) with Dict(Str, Object) anywhere (a callee that writes a\nstr into its parameter) moves every Dict(Str, Int) in the program into\nthe (Str, Object) store, and a chain of such joins can make most dicts\ndynamic. Correct, but it loses typed storage for dicts that never meet.\nClasses keyed by creation site (the literal or constructor that made\nthe dict) would keep them apart.","files":null}]}